            <ArticleTitle>Medical issues in treating renal transplant patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-2, 55-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>As the survival of renal transplant patients has increased, so has their risk of significant morbidity. Immunosuppressive drugs can exacerbate preexisting conditions and promote development of new disease. Effective long-term care of transplant recipients requires an understanding of how these drugs affect clinical evaluations and treatments.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
